def check_bit_difference(a, b):
    # Check if both numbers are equal
    if a == b:
        return False

    # Find the position of the first different bit
    for i in range(len(bin(a)[2:])):
        if bin(a)[2:].index('1') != bin(b)[2:].index('1'):
            return True

    # If no different bit is found, they are equal
    return False
```

```python
def differ_at_one_bit_position(a, b):
    if a == b:
        return False
    for i in range(31, -1, -1):
        if (a >> i) & 1 != (b >> i) & 1:
            return True
    return False
```

This function works by iterating through the bits of the numbers from the least significant bit to the most significant bit. If any pair of bits differs at one position, it immediately returns True. If it goes through all 31 bits without finding a difference, it returns False.

